  <h2 id="psychiatry-track">The psychiatry route in full</h2>

  <p>
    If you are leaning toward staying on the medical route, here is the complete stage-by-stage runway, not just the headline "become a doctor" version.
  </p>

  <p class="note-line">
    The math behind the 9-12 year range: MBBS runs about 5.5 years including internship, and MD Psychiatry adds 3 more - roughly 8.5 years if you clear NEET-PG on your first attempt. Most aspirants need one or more extra years of NEET-PG preparation given the competition for a psychiatry seat, which is what stretches the realistic range closer to 10-12 years for many students.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
