        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">What the actual workweek looks like</p>
    <p>
      An MD Psychiatry resident's week runs through ward rounds, medication management, on-call duty, and patient files across a hospital's psychiatry unit - broad clinical medicine first, with mental health as the specialisation layered on top, not the whole job from day one.
    </p>
    <p>
      Junior residents at government and central institutes typically earn Rs 55,000-95,000 a month during training, rising to Rs 1,00,000-1,50,000 a month for senior residents. A full psychiatrist's average pay sits near Rs 15 lakh a year, with a wide reported range of roughly Rs 3.4-29.3 lakh depending on setting, city, and years of practice - verify current figures against live listings rather than treating any single number as fixed.
    </p>
  </div>

