    <p>
      An RCI-regulated MA Clinical Psychology trainee's week runs through supervised therapy sessions, psychometric testing, case-note writing, and clinical supervision meetings - sustained one-on-one work, with no prescribing authority at any point, even after full registration.
    </p>
    <p>
      Fresh MA-RCI graduates at private hospitals often start near Rs 15,000-25,000 a month, while RCI-registered psychologists at government institutes like NIMHANS or AIIMS report in-hand pay of Rs 80,000-95,000 a month with experience. For the full six-track breakdown across clinical, counselling, organisational psychology, research, UX research, and people analytics, see <a href="/blog/career-options/career-in-psychology-india-salary-scope/">career in psychology India salary scope</a>.
    </p>
